{
  "_limits_note": "D6 bounds (Plan v2.3 / FW-2): axes <= 8, buttons <= 128, encoders <= 4 -- totals across direct + ADS1115 + matrix + expander kinds. Direct-pin buttons are pin-limited to 11 anyway; 128 is reachable only via button_matrix / expanders. batteries <= 1 (one supply per board); led_strips <= 1, <= 60 LEDs per strip (WS2812). The old buttons limit (32) was the pre-D6 direct-only bound.",
  "_note": "ADC2 pins (0,2,4,12,13,14,15,25,26,27) are unusable for analog while Wi-Fi is on, hence adc=null. Verify on the real board before freezing (F0 exit).",
  "_presets_note": "Presets are validated by tests-host/pin_rules_ref.py (single source of truth). The direct full rig fits only because GPIO21 is used as a digital LED pin (R-L9); with expanders, 21/22 are I2C and the LED moves to a freed digital pin (GPIO4 in the MCP23017 preset).",
